{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' answer/launch_recommendation.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Checkpoint 3: Final Launch Recommendation\n\nRecommend these three first-wave clinics:\n\n| Clinic | Clinic ID | Carrier | Delivery Date | Total Rollout Cost |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: |\n| Maple Junction Clinic | N-101 | SwiftRoute | 2026-06-06 | `$7,400` |\n| Riverbend Health | N-102 | NorthLine | 2026-06-07 | `$6,450` |\n| Hillcrest Annex | N-106 | Valley Freight | 2026-06-07 | `$4,950` |\n\nThese are the only three clinics that satisfy every hard requirement in the current first-wave rules: North region, open status during the 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14 launch window, accepted effective storage status, full coordinator coverage, delivery by 2026-06-07, and total cost within budget.\n\nTotal rollout cost: `$18,800`\n\nRemaining budget: `$1,200`\n\nAnchor clinic and donor continuity code: Maple Junction Clinic remains eligible and should be retained as the donor continuity anchor. Donor continuity code: `MJ-14`.\n\nRejected-clinic summary:\n\n- Pine Ridge Outreach was blocked because Lena Torres is unavailable on 2026-06-12, so coordinator coverage is not full-window.\n- Lakeside Family Care was blocked because its storage status is `suspended` after the 2026-05-06 storage update.\n- Cedar Works Clinic was blocked because the clinic is `closed maintenance`; its quoted delivery date of 2026-06-08 also misses the first-wave cutoff.\n- Old Mill Clinic was blocked because its storage status remains `conditional pass pending`, which is not accepted for first-wave use.\n- South Gate Clinic was excluded because it is in the South region, outside the North-region first-wave scope.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
